{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470345-transformative-power-of-vitae","id":1470345,"title":"Transformative power of Vitae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-13T07:50:51-08:00","id":1470345,"title":"Transformative power of Vitae","content":"Since Nosferatu can breed alligators that are larger and more feral in appearance than normal by nurturing them with Vitae ( Nosferatu clanbook ), in your opinion can a ghoul do the same? Use Vitae to grow larger and monstrous ( mabye by taking the Huge Size merit and the Monstrous flaw ) ?<br /> <br /> Also, the alligator ( reptile buddy merit ) had 2 dots in Potence and Fortitude regardless of his master's generation.<br /> <br /> Mabye a ghoul could achieve the same if he mutated and enlarged his body by feeding on a lot of Vitae for years? <br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> Since ghouls can, through a great Willpower effort, regrow body parts...<br /> could it be possible to surgically harvest muscular tissue, keep it alive in lab vats, regrow the tissue with Vitae, then auto-transplant muscular fibers to enlarge and enhance mass?<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> By feeding on Gangrel's vitae, may it be possible for a ghoul to reproduce <b>permanent</b> feral mutations? Mabye by learning Protean and applying it creatively?<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Bodybuilding is, basically, to create micro-wounds in the muscles ( and , in lesser extent, bones ) who heal reinforcing the pre-existing tissue.<br /> Since a ghoul can use Vitae to heal, if he had a steady reserve avaiable, could it be used to enhance strength and bone density above the normal human limits ( by repeated crash training that would cripple a normal human ) ?<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> One of Vicissitude modifications allows a ghoul to eat and digest any kind of organic matter - and most inorganic ones too.<br /> Could something similar be done to allow a modified ghoul to turn human blood into Vitae?<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> Revenant are able to produce their own weak Vitae. If the source of that Vitae is located ( spinal marrow? spleen? ) could some tissue be harvested and transplanted to give a similar ability to a normal ghoul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T09:41:14-08:00","id":1470348,"title":"","content":"Mostly no. <br /> <br /> Animals get swole from Vitae, I think it's stated the growth effect is most pronounced with arthropods and other bugs, which may give the impression that the further away from human, the more visible the effects are. Perhaps getting swole is due to a decreased effeciency in using vitae; Potence in vampires is 100% something which increases power without visible changes to muscles, while Potence in animals is imperfect/impure/has some conversion difficulties and, well, let's imagine mamals are 80% stronger and 20% more muscular, reptiles and birds are 50/50, and fish are 80/20. Something to that effect. <br /> <br /> One important thing that writers have stressed about Vitae is that it's got some serious &quot;stasis&quot; properties. It prevents or slows growth. Using it to repair muscles will just have it repair them to the state before they were torn. IE all your attempts at gains were for nothing. Ditto with bone density.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T16:23:37-08:00","id":1470385,"title":"","content":"Basically the game have a lot of thrown around instances of Vitae being used to create Resident Evil-like mutations on animals and plants, but never cared to give a system for this, imply a system in lore, much less let this happen to humans. You can only experiment with feeding vitae to something, watch what happens, note it down and roughly expect the experiment to have consistent results with a similar subject, but no predictive effect for other subjects.<br /> <br /> Revenants have already been created by centuries of experimentation by the Tzimisce. If it was possible to induce a regular Ghoul to become a Revenant, they would already know how to. But remember that a Revenant can actually <i>also</i> be a Ghoul anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T04:52:26-08:00","id":1470420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470345-transformative-power-of-vitae?p=1470348#post1470348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One important thing that writers have stressed about Vitae is that it's got some serious &quot;stasis&quot; properties. It prevents or slows growth. Using it to repair muscles will just have it repair them to the state before they were torn. IE all your attempts at gains were for nothing. Ditto with bone density.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a slightly more accurate read is thaf Vitae has the properties of stolen life force. The stasis manifests in the form of keeping alive that which should be dead while, for those things still living, it instead adds to their life force (i.e. why ghouls universally pick up Potence and have their emotions heightened).<br /> <br /> Where this presents an interesting course is in the transition\u2026 when the ghoul lives past their mortal lifespan they become entirely dependent upon Vitae to keep themselves alive\u2026 they become closer to being a vampire.<br /> <br /> I would argue that if you wanted to play up the horror of the Vitae, allow the things like excessive growth and development, but only during the mortal\u2019s normal lifespan\u2026 then once they become dependent upon Vitae for life let not just a stasis, but a hollowing out occur as they are literally only sustained by the small amounts of Vitae their masters allow them to feed upon. The free dot of Potence fades (unless the ghoul spent XP to actually develop a real dot of it) because the Vitae is no longer adding life force to the living but sustaining what would now be a corpse without it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}